[36m(TaskRunner pid=3939378)[0m 3. **Magnification Formula**:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3939378)[0m    The magnification \(M\) of a telescope is given by the ratio of the focal length of the objective lens to the focal length of the eyepiece. However, since we are not given the focal length of the eyepiece, we can use the angular diameter formula for a telescope:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3939378)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3939378)[0m    \text{Angular size of the image} = \frac{\text{Angular size of the object}}{\text{Magnification}}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3939378)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3939378)[0m    The magnification \(M\) can also be expressed as the ratio of the focal length of the objective lens to the focal length of the eyepiece, but since we don't have the eyepiece focal length, we can use the angular size formula directly:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3939378)[0m    \[
