[36m(TaskRunner pid=3939378)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3939378)[0m    The angular size of the image in radians is also given by:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3939378)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3939378)[0m    \text{Angular size of the image} = \frac{\text{Diameter of the image}}{\text{Distance to the image}}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3939378)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=3939378)[0m    Since the telescopes are observing the planet at its distance, the distance to the image is essentially the focal length of the telescopes, which is \(72 \text{ m}\). So:
